class:: HPCPCrest
summary:: Peak-to-average pitch-class strength
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Computes N*max(chroma)/sum(chroma). This general crest statistic distinguishes concentrated from diffuse pitch-class evidence. Silence returns zero, a uniform nonzero vector gives one, and one occupied class gives N. It is gain invariant and does not infer a key.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chroma
A C-first Array of 12, 24, 36, or 120 nonnegative pitch-class values. Higher resolutions fold to nearest semitones where a twelve-class representation is required.

argument:: trig
A positive value processes this control block. For FFT-derived features pass chain >= 0 so each analysis frame is used once; default 1 processes each control block.

returns::
Crest factor from 1 through N on nonzero input; zero for silence.

examples::
HPCPCrest calculates the peak-to-average crest factor of pitch-class distribution (from 1 for uniform equal distribution up to 12 for energy concentrated in a single pitch class). In this example, pitch-class crest factor controls an audio-rate resonant feedback comb filter, cleanly sustaining pure single notes while relaxing during complex chords. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: displays real-time HPCP crest factor.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("piano-chords.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic chords fallback
            Mix.ar(SinOsc.ar([261.63, 329.63, 392.00, 523.25] * LFNoise0.kr(0.5).range(1, 1.25))) * 0.15
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var chroma = HPCP.kr(chain, size: 12, harmonics: 2, normalize: \max, fftSize: 2048);
        var crest = HPCPCrest.kr(chroma, chain >= 0);
        var crestLag = crest.lag(0.08);
        var resQ = crestLag.linlin(1, 8, 0.1, 0.8).clip(0.1, 0.9);
        var filtered = RLPF.ar(source, 200 + (crestLag * 400), 1 - resQ) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + (filtered ! 2);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, crestLag.clip(1, 12)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("HPCP Crest Factor", ~miraBus, 1.0, 12.0, "crest");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
